
|WKBDESCRIPTION
============|YKO

Combatbrief allows you to customize various aspects of the way combat
messages are displayed. Each toggle is its own setting. It is
possible to have all, none, or a few toggled on at a time.

|YKBcombatbrief        |WKO- |YKODisplays your current combatbrief status

|YKBcombatbrief short  |WKO- |YKOAll combat messages are displayed as 'A hits B' or
                     'A misses B'

|YKBcombatbrief self   |WKO- |YKOOnly attacks by or against you will be displayed.

|YKBcombatbrief hit    |WKO- |YKOOnly hits will be displayed. Dodges and misses will
                     be ignored.
                    
|YKBcombatbrief damage |WKO- |YKODamage numbers will be shown at the end of your combat
                     messages. This setting is available at any level and
                     is on by default.

|YKBcombatbrief visual |WKO- |YKOWhen a compatible Darkflow Combat pane is ready,
                     routine weapon swings are shown visually instead of
                     filling the terminal. If the pane or client is not
                     ready, normal combat messages continue automatically.
                     This setting is enabled by default for new characters.

Visual mode is independent of short, self, hit, and damage. The self and hit
filters still decide which exchanges reach the pane, while damage decides
whether exact numbers are shown. Screenreader combat summaries take priority.

Closing or collapsing the Combat pane restores terminal combat messages
without changing your saved visual preference. Triggers, highlights, and
client logs that depend on routine swing text will not receive those replaced
lines while the visual pane is active.
